  title: Chinese New Year Celebrations 19th Century
  info: "Singapore\u2019s Chinese community celebrates the Lunar New Year with family
    reunions, lion dances, and the exchange of red packets symbolizing good fortune.
    Signature customs include yusheng (prosperity toss) and decorating homes with
    red lanterns. The vibrant festivities reflect Chinese cultural traditions and
    their integration into Singaporean society."
